    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm planning a big corporate gala for like 500 people next month and just got a bunch of last minute emails about nut allergies and some vegan guests. how should i best communicate this to the catering team and what's the best way to label the buffet so people don't accidentally eat something they shouldn't? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Contact the catering team immediately and clearly explain the situation, specifying the number of nut-allergic guests, the requirements for vegan guests, and emphasizing the importance of labeling clearly to avoid cross-contamination. Provide a detailed written list of guests' dietary restrictions and communicate the urgency of these last-minute changes.\n\nOn the buffet table, create separate sections for different dietary needs with clear, bold labels such as \"Nut-Free,\" \"Vegan,\" and \"Gluten-Free,\" if necessary, beside each food item. Consider also using colored tableware that reflects these categories to further assist guests in identifying suitable options. Place large posters or signs at the entrance and entrance points to dietary sections as spot reminders for guests.",
