    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds okay, but i'm actually really worried about the kitchen staff missing something during the rush. like, how do i make sure the chefs themselves are actually following these protocols and not just skimming the list? is there a specific way to format the instructions so nothing gets overlooked in the heat of service?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To guarantee compliance from the kitchen staff, you must ensure they are thoroughly briefed on the importance of these dietary restrictions. Arrange a briefing session with all the chefs and prep staff before the event, where you clearly discuss each chef's responsibilities. Use visual aids like charts or infographics to highlight critical points. Consider implementing a colour-coded tagging system on the prep sheets for different dietary needs, which can be fast visual references for the chefs even during the rush.\n\nCreate a laminated document that lists all the dietary restrictions with corresponding examples and provide it to key staff members. This document should be easily accessible in the kitchen and on the prep tables. Additionally, request that the chefs undergo a final check-off each time they prepare meals to ensure every dish complies with the set guidelines. Leave no details behind by reinforcing the high stakes of allergen cross-contamination and the potential consequences for guests' health.\n\nFinally, arrange for a designated, trained dietary manager or a special diet coordinator to oversee recipes and cooking cross-sections. This individual responsible for coordinating between the kitchen, catering team, and events staff will ensure that operational hiccups are addressed and proper communication remains the standard protocol throughout the service period. Continuous communication channels such as a dedicated communication device line or radio channel to",
      "source": "target",
